# Grid B — U1 Security audit (command injection surface)
#
# Gap target: no security_audit scenario exists (see scenario.go
# comments referencing aspirational security_audit / refactor_design
# that were never wired). This case measures whether the pipeline
# can reach a taint-source → sink answer via the architecture_explain
# fallback path.
#
# Ground truth (internal/tool/builtin.go:108): ExecCommand.Execute
# shells out via the exec_command tool. The relevant audit question
# is whether user input paths can reach exec_command without
# sanitization, and the known defense is that REPL requests are
# passed as --request arg, not into a shell pipeline.
#
# Positive anchor pins the tool name the audit must be scoped to.
# Negative anchors block the "no risk" brush-off and the opposite
# "sql injection" hallucination from training-distribution leakage
# (codrax has no database).
ID="u1a"
NAME="security audit — exec_command injection surface"
QUESTION="codrax 的 exec_command 工具是否存在命令注入风险？请给出实际的 taint source 和 sink，以及现有的防护点。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC was just `exec_command`
# (the tool name in the question) — answer "Yes exec_command has
# injection risk" PASSed without naming taint source / sink /
# defense. Strengthen by requiring the answer to surface the THREE
# security-audit pillars explicitly: taint (source), sink, and
# defense / 防护. Allow English or Chinese phrasing.
# 2026-05-08 broaden: model rendered the tool name in Go-CamelCase
# `ExecCommand` / `execCommandParams` (the Go type/struct names) rather
# than the registry literal `exec_command`. Both refer to the same
# tool — the registry name uses snake_case, the Go implementation uses
# CamelCase by convention. Move the tool-name anchor into regex with
# alternation so either form satisfies it.
EXPECT_CONTAINS=""
# 2026-05-09 second-pass broaden: regex is run via grep -E (case-
# sensitive). Model wrote "Taint Source" / "Taint Sink" with capital
# T (natural English title-case for security-audit prose) but the
# regex `taint` lowercase-only didn't match. Same for sink (Sink
# capital). Use [Tt]aint / [Ss]ink charset alternations so both
# cases match.
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(exec_command|ExecCommand|execCommand)
([Tt]aint|污点|输入)
([Ss]ink|执行点|shell|外部.*命令)
(defense|sanitize|whitelist|防护|过滤|清洗)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="no.risk SQL.injection sql"
